        "### Experiment 1: Vector and Matrix Operations for Deep Learning\n",
        "\n",
        "**Problem Statement:**\n",
        "An e-commerce bookstore represents customers and products as numeric vectors to power its recommendation engine. We have:\n",
        "- **6 customers** and **5 genres** (Customer-Genre rating matrix: $6 \\times 5$)\n",
        "- **5 genres** and **4 books** (Genre-Book weights matrix: $5 \\times 4$)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Tasks:**\n",
        "1. Build the Customer-Genre ($6 \\times 5$) and Genre-Book ($5 \\times 4$) matrices in NumPy.\n",
        "2. Compute dot products, matrix product, transpose, inverse (if valid), and element-wise operations.\n",
        "3. Compute cosine similarity between customers and identify the two most similar.\n",
        "4. Show that a dense layer is $y = Wx + b$ by computing it manually for one customer.\n",
        "5. Visualize the score matrix as a heatmap."
      ]
    },
